At midday, Jonas and I take a break.
We set off together.
We walk quickly down the street.
Soon we see a small bakery.
We go inside and get in line.
"Hello," says the shop assistant.
"What would you like?" she asks.
"I would like a crusty Brötchen, please," I say.
"And a coffee."
The Brötchen and the coffee cost four euros fifty.
I pay at the till.
Jonas also buys his lunch.
Then we sit down at a small table.
We eat and chat.
"How is your project going, Maya?" asks Jonas.
"It is going well," I answer.
After half an hour we go back to the office.
